[TEXT] **Critical anomaly found in router0's routing table:**

```
K>* 1.0.0.0/8 [0/0] via 127.0.0.1, lo       ← SELECTED (AD=0, blackholes Server Room traffic)
R   1.0.0.0/8 [120/3] via 10.10.0.2, eth2   ← NOT selected (RIP route shadowed)
R>* 128.168.0.0/16 [120/3] via 10.10.0.2     ← selected correctly (Internet Lab works)
```

A kernel-injected route (`K`, AD=0) for `1.0.0.0/8` points to `127.0.0.1` (loopback), completely overriding the correct RIP route. This is the "temporary backup route". Let me confirm the blackhole and inspect the running config.
